Package: xpam
Type: Package
Title: Presence-Absence Matrix Construction from Species Range Maps
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Angel", "Robles",
           email = "a.l.robles.fernandez@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4559-1751"))
Description: Constructs presence-absence matrices (PAMs) from species
    range polygons or occurrence records.  A streaming native engine
    rasterizes geometries onto a user-defined grid or bins them in
    environmental space, and returns the sites-by-species incidence as a
    sparse matrix plus marginals; a native Jaccard backend computes
    species-by-species or site-by-site similarity directly from the same
    incidence, at scale.  A small-input dense path is kept for
    convenience.  Includes convenience functions to retrieve example
    mammal range data and WorldClim environmental layers projected to
    two dimensions via Principal Component Analysis.
